  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Sodium levofolinate, the active form of folinic acid, is used to treat megaloblastic anemia and as a detoxifying (rescue) agent alongside anticancer treatment. It is an approved medicine and is included on the WHO list of essential medicines, so it is widely available.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q192464\">Wikidata Q192464</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>sodium levofolinate</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>V03AF10</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=\"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB11596\">DB11596</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=\"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/149436\">149436</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=\"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:63606\">63606</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q192464\">Q192464</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C20H23N7O7</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>473.439 g/mol (knowledgebase (DrugBank calculated))</td></tr></table><p><small>Drugs.Common 25.09 gave 517.4 g/mol (+9.3 %); replaced by the value above</small></p></body></html>"));
